<title>UK: Clyde Blowers wins contracts from China.</title>
<headline>Clyde Blowers wins contracts from China.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering group Clyde Blowers Plc said on Friday that it has won two ash handling contracts from China.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the contracts have been valued independently at over two million stg each.</p>
<p>The contracts, which are to provide ash handling systems for five 350MW boilers, were won from China Electric Power and The Shanghai Electric Power Corp.</p>
<p>London Newsroom + 44 171 542 4019</p>
